BLOCK 21 -- THE ABSORPTION CURVE: how does damage scale with the NUMBER
            of wrong anchors, and does DIRECTION matter as well as SIZE?
================================================================================================
  [floor, 2*sd/mean] eval-draw 5.5% | calibration-draw 1.5% | (superseded range stat 11.1%)
  Two facts sit far apart and the shape between them is unmeasured:
    a MINORITY of receivers displaced is LARGELY ABSORBED by the
      intercept fit. HOW MUCH depends on WHICH receivers, and the
      table below measures exactly that. An earlier version of this
      header quoted a single figure from a side measurement; the
      f=7 row below supersedes it and they disagree.
    ALL receivers wrong by the estimator own median error: about +464%
  If the curve is LINEAR, coordinate error is additive. If it has a KNEE,
  C1 is a COLLAPSE phenomenon and a practitioner who gets most gateways
  roughly right is safe while one who gets them all wrong is not.
  NOTE: this block NEVER mutates PHYS or RSSF. Every corrupted map is a
  new dict, and A0 is refitted on it so each map is self-consistent.

